01:05:01.640 --> 01:05:04.480
to pursue some sensible
democratic political reforms,

01:05:04.480 --> 01:05:06.410
small d democratic political reforms.

01:05:06.410 --> 01:05:11.410
And to me, everyone knows
what the big ones should be.

01:05:12.170 --> 01:05:13.720
It's not court packing.

01:05:13.720 --> 01:05:16.030
It's not Puerto Rico and DC statehood

01:05:16.030 --> 01:05:20.210
though, I would be
supportive of the latter.

01:05:20.210 --> 01:05:23.260
It's making sure that every
American has the right to vote

01:05:23.260 --> 01:05:25.750
and that politicians are prevented

01:05:25.750 --> 01:05:27.980
or at least have reduced capacity

01:05:27.980 --> 01:05:32.040
to choose their voters rather
than voters choosing them

01:05:32.040 --> 01:05:34.480
through extreme partisan gerrymandering.

01:05:34.480 --> 01:05:39.180
So the prospects for
those things are dismal.

01:05:39.180 --> 01:05:41.960
But I think, one thing that
Democrats should recognize is

01:05:41.960 --> 01:05:46.130
that fighting the good fight
is sometimes good politics too.

01:05:46.130 --> 01:05:48.150
I would push for these

01:05:48.150 --> 01:05:50.540
and I think that's why
Senate control is crucial.

01:05:50.540 --> 01:05:53.300
Is Joe Manchin gonna prevent?

01:05:53.300 --> 01:05:55.580
I mean, my public option
does not look to have

01:05:55.580 --> 01:05:58.770
