01:15:08.710 --> 01:15:12.480
this two and a half, whatever
month transition system.

01:15:12.480 --> 01:15:14.670
it is a little strange, isn't it?

01:15:14.670 --> 01:15:17.360
Isabella, could you just put
this in comparative perspective

01:15:17.360 --> 01:15:20.040
and then David, anyone
else who wants to comment

01:15:20.040 --> 01:15:21.360
that would be great.

01:15:21.360 --> 01:15:22.727
- I'm Looking for (mumbles).

01:15:23.790 --> 01:15:25.560
I'm not an expert on American politics.

01:15:25.560 --> 01:15:28.810
It seems to me, isn't this a
legacy of the electoral college

01:15:28.810 --> 01:15:31.120
and the fact that you
had this institutions

01:15:31.120 --> 01:15:34.801
where they had to gather
together and sort of come.

01:15:34.801 --> 01:15:37.293
So it's just this historical
accident I think kind of

01:15:37.293 --> 01:15:39.530
that is connected to the electoral college

01:15:39.530 --> 01:15:43.193
that sort of creates
this kind of lag that we-

01:15:48.683 --> 01:15:53.340
- Yes, so I think
Isabella's frozen not me.

01:15:53.340 --> 01:15:54.440
Is Isabella frozen?

01:15:54.440 --> 01:15:56.750
Okay, it's usually me.

01:15:56.750 --> 01:15:59.410
- I'm sure Christina or David
can tell the difference.

01:15:59.410 --> 01:16:00.500
- David, do you wanna jump in

01:16:00.500 --> 01:16:03.878
and then Isabella can catch
up or Christina comments.

01:16:03.878 --> 01:16:07.910
- (mumbles) and you know what
has happened to these efforts

01:16:07.910 --> 01:16:10.640
historically, because probably we're not

01:16:10.640 --> 01:16:13.890
